# NG-RT-REFRACTION-NIGHT: the night half of NG-RT-REFRACTION.scn (designs S:/aftmp/NG-RT-REFRACTION3H-DESIGN.md,
# S:/aftmp/NG-RT-REFRACTION3G-DESIGN.md,
# S:/aftmp/NG-RT-REFRACTION3E-DESIGN.md, F:/aftmp/NG-RT-REFRACTION3D-DESIGN.md, F:/aftmp/NG-RT-REFRACTION3C-DESIGN.md
# and F:/aftmp/NG-RT-REFRACTION3-DESIGN.md, «## Приёмка»; physics F:/aftmp/NG-RT-REFRACTION2-DESIGN.md). One editor
# session in F:/BistroFoliageProj, GI_Bistro_Night: the shop window as path tracer | Translucency.Refraction
# ScreenSpace | HardwareTraced | HardwareTraced with the composite off | ScreenSpace again | HardwareTraced again | HardwareTraced with
# Reflections.HitLighting 1 | with one interface bend - one camera, one exposure, one time, one tier.
# The pass cost (3H Q6): "Translucency: Ray Traced Refraction" read 2.008 ms day at 1787x657 = 1.17 Mpx with the
# path end from the cards (the day_rt dump, editor.log:16575 of scn-1128-135823), 2.561 ms with it lit in place (the
# refr_split dump, :19475), 0.180 ms muted (:18061). 3H leaves one branch (lit in place) and one budget: the pass
# <= 3.0 ms at 1.17 Mpx, held once, by [rt_reset] of NG-RT-REFRACTION.scn for the day and by [refr_pass] here for the
# night dump only. The pass numbers are read from editor.log of the run folder: the reply files
# line_NNN_profile-dump.txt are empty ({"id":1,"ok":true}).
# What is behind the glass (3H): there is NO interior in this content (0 BistroInterior entities, 0 interior
# meshes); behind the shop window stands the empty shell of the building (the underside of the slab
# Paris_Building_01_paris_building_01_4279 behind the upper right sash). Raster and path tracer show the SAME
# surfaces behind the glass - never "an interior". The window is the closed pair _4711 (outward) + _4875 (inward);
# the duplicate _4713 is gone from the content (3H D1). This half deletes no glass; a step that ever does deletes
# the pair together, never one sheet (one sheet reads green over the whole pane, 3H D7).
# One branch (3H D3): the end of a refraction path is lit in place at every tier, whatever Reflections.HitLighting
# says; night_rt is HitLighting 0 (High), refr_split HitLighting 1 of one camera - the two are equal within the run
# noise (night_rt vs night_rt_b), and so are their pass times.
# The path tracer is the reference: GlobalIllumination + Reflections PathTraced (the tracer pairs them). The raster
# frames keep Reflections / GI HardwareTraced; only the Translucency rows change between night_ss, night_rt and
# night_rt_mute.
# The tier (D7): every group of the preset is pinned at High before any row (a group level drops that group's rows,
# so the pins come first); the benchmark preset chooses nothing in this run. Reflections.TranslucentFrontLayer is
# not set here (High = 1): the night isolates the refraction; the day proves D1. An unattended run keeps every
# Quality change in this process (QualityState::KeepInSession): machine.json is never written; the tail still
# clears the rows. There is no group "Level" command: the next run starts from the machine's own selection.
# A/B order (D8, D9; 3C; 3G D6): night_ss -> night_rt -> night_rt_mute -> night_ss_b -> night_rt_b -> refr_split
# -> night_rt_mi1 with the camera still, 256 frames each, and only then the two 16-frame turns (D10); night_ss vs
# night_ss_b (ScreenSpace twice, night_rt and night_rt_mute between them) is the drift of the scenario itself over
# the interval night_rt_mute is compared across. The opaque pixels of [night_rt] (3D D4): |night_rt - night_ss|
# not above the larger of the two repeats |night_ss - night_ss_b| and |night_rt - night_rt_b| - a bound taken from one
# side of the comparison measures that side's noise (5.66 against 5.09 and 7.81 in scn-1128-095738).
# night_rt_mute: HardwareTraced with Translucency.RefractionComposite 0 (the glass cell ignores the trace): its
# opaque pixels vs night_ss show whether the pass's graph reads move them (D9). Its opaque pixels (3G D6) are the
# pixels black in night_front, the glass layer of the frame: under the composite off EVERY glass of the frame
# (the neighbouring windows, the lamp shades) shows the scene copy, so "outside the pane rectangle" counts glass as
# opaque (9.45 against the bound 6.26 in scn-1128-114614, while night_rt vs night_ss read 3.01). The editor has no
# view mode drawing the glass layer yet, so night_front is a statement, EXPECTED RED, and the mask stays the
# rectangle's outside until it exists (3G D6 open).
# The knockout of [night_rt] (3C D1): night_rt_b is HardwareTraced again after night_ss_b, the camera still
# (the run noise); |night_rt - night_rt_mute| >= 2 x |night_rt - night_rt_b|, mean |delta| of (R+G+B)/3 (0..255)
# over the pane mask = rectangle x540-1260 y170-630, pixels where night_pt > 8 (KO3C-NIGHT: 5.42 against 7.43 -
# the trace's answer never reached the frame once the interface budget ran out). night_rt_mi1 is HardwareTraced
# with Translucency.RefractionMaxInterfaces 1: the budget bounds the bends, not the answer, so the glass differs
# from night_rt_mute at least as much as night_rt does.
# The window rule (D6): a GPU time is a budget number only when the window is free - in BOTH dumps of a pair (ss
# and rt) "ClearMainFramebuffer" <= 0.2 ms, and their "GPU frame" differ by less than 2x; else the number is not
# a measurement and the run is repeated. Budget at 1080p = ms x 2073600 / (viewport width x height), the
# viewport size from editor.log (1787x657 today = 1.17 Mpx). Every measured capture has its own profile-dump
# (reply line_NNN_profile-dump.txt) right before it.
# Frame wait: `frames N` (N presented frames). Every compared capture stands >= 256 frames after the last
# GlobalIllumination.Method switch or camera turn (GI accumulation converged; else the opaque pixels drift).
# The camera faces the cafe shop window Bistro_Research_Exterior_Paris_Building_01_paris_building_01_bottom_4711
# (MASTER_Glass_Exterior, StaticMeshGlass; pane pivot -108,197,-719, centre ~y 320) from 3 m out on the terrace.
# One exposure: AutoExposure off (at the scene's own ManualExposureEV100), back on in the tail.
Проект ../BistroFoliageProj/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/GI_Bistro_Night.desce
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Textures High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Filtering High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Shadows High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: GlobalIllumination High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Reflections High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: PostProcess High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Effects High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: ViewDistance High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: AntiAliasing High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: ResolutionScale High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Shading High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: PathTracing High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Foliage High"
Дано run Anti-Aliasing "Anti-Aliasing: TAA"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Resolution.Percent 100"
# The profile-dumps carry GPU times only with GPU profiling on (Profiler "GPU"; off, every scope reads gpu 0.000).
Дано run Debug "GPU profiling: On"
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position -370,300,-861
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.8806,0.07,0.4738
Дано set 6039035132485441499 PostProcessVolumeData.Settings.AutoExposure false
# --- night: path tracer | ScreenSpace | HardwareTraced | HardwareTraced, composite off - the camera does not move
Когда run Quality "Quality: GlobalIllumination.Method PathTraced"
Когда run Quality "Quality: Reflections.Method PathTraced"
Когда frames 256
Тогда-вид night_pt night, path tracer, the duplicate sheet _4713 gone from the scene: the reference - behind the glass the empty shell of the building (the underside of the slab 4279 behind the upper right sash) as the night light reaches it
Когда run Quality "Quality: GlobalIllumination.Method HardwareTraced"
Когда run Quality "Quality: Reflections.Method HardwareTraced"
Когда run Quality "Quality: Translucency.Refraction ScreenSpace"
Когда frames 256
Когда profile-dump
Тогда-вид night_ss night, ScreenSpace: the A side of every comparison - mean L of the glass area vs night_pt recorded; profile-dump: the window rule (ClearMainFramebuffer <= 0.2 ms)
Когда run Quality "Quality: Translucency.Refraction HardwareTraced"
Когда frames 256
Когда profile-dump
Тогда refr_pass "Translucency: Ray Traced Refraction" in the night_rt dump (read in editor.log, see the head; the day dumps are held by [rt_reset] of NG-RT-REFRACTION.scn): GPU time non-zero and <= 3.0 ms at 1787x657 = 1.17 Mpx (3H Q6, the path end lit in place; 2.561 ms day in place in scn-1128-135823), the number and its 1080p scaling (ms x 2073600 / viewport width x height) named; the window holds by the rule (ClearMainFramebuffer <= 0.2 ms in the night_ss and night_rt dumps, their GPU frame within 2x)
Тогда-вид night_rt night, HardwareTraced: differs from night_ss only inside the glass pixels; opaque pixels: |night_rt − night_ss| not above the larger of |night_ss − night_ss_b| and |night_rt − night_rt_b| (5.66 against 5.09 and 7.81 in scn-1128-095738); behind the glass the same surfaces of the empty shell as in night_pt, no black underside; night_rt vs night_rt_mute on the glass at least 2x night_rt vs night_rt_b (mean |delta| over the pane mask, see the head)
# --- the mask of the opaque pixels of night_rt_mute (3G D6)
Тогда night_front night, HardwareTraced, the camera of night_rt: EXPECTED RED - the glass layer of the frame (every glass pixel: the pane, the neighbouring windows, the lamp shades) is the mask of the opaque pixels of night_rt_mute (black = opaque); the editor has no view mode drawing the glass layer (the "View mode:" list of ViewportCommands.cpp has none), so until it exists the opaque pixels stay the outside of the pane rectangle x540-1260 y170-630 and 3G D6 stays open, named
Когда run Quality "Quality: Translucency.RefractionComposite 0"
Когда frames 256
Когда profile-dump
Тогда-вид night_rt_mute night, HardwareTraced, composite off (Translucency.RefractionComposite 0): the opaque pixels by the night_front mask (while it has no view mode: the outside of the pane rectangle) against night_ss, mean |delta| <= max(|night_ss − night_ss_b| over the same pixels, 6.26) (9.45 against 6.26 in scn-1128-114614); the 3G D6 experiment: scripts/Dev/frames_compare.py night_rt_mute.png night_ss.png diff.png - the bounding box of the difference outside the pane written down: on glass, the mask's defect (night_front); on walls, the GI drift night_ss_b bounds; if neither, the cause of D9 is the pass's reads in the graph and the feature goes back to the architect with this frame; profile-dump vs night_rt: the composite's share (D11)
Когда run Quality "Quality: Translucency.RefractionComposite Level"
